# Copy to frontend/.env.local (git-ignored) only to point a local build at another backend.
#
# Vite variables (VITE_*) are PUBLIC: they are baked into the JavaScript at build time and anyone
# can read them in the browser. Put the backend's URL here, never a secret (no API key, no rep or
# admin token).

# The backend's public URL, e.g. https://compass-api.onrender.com (no trailing slash, no /api).
# Every fetch and SSE call goes to it (src/api/client.ts). Empty (the default): the same origin,
# which is what dev uses (Vite proxies /api to the API on :8000) and the local single-origin demo
# (tasks.py demo). Deployed, render.yaml sets it for the compass-web static site, and its CSP
# (connect-src, also in render.yaml) must name the same URL.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
